          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Industry context</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">OT/IT convergence creates new operational risk</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Power generation, water treatment and oil and gas facilities rely on SCADA systems that were traditionally air-gapped. As operators integrate these systems with enterprise IT for real-time analytics and remote management, the attack surface expands significantly. SCADA, DNP3, and GOOSE protocols — critical for grid operations — require protocol-aware monitoring that standard IT security tools cannot provide.</p>
          <p>Across the region, smart grid modernisation is accelerating, with renewable energy integration demanding real-time monitoring and dynamic load balancing. Protecting operational technology requires specialised approaches — industrial network segmentation, zero-trust access controls, and OT-specific protocol visibility. National cybersecurity agencies in the Gulf are mandating critical infrastructure protection frameworks that align with international ICS security standards.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

